<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŏrĭbundus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		morior. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Dying</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">minus valet, moribundus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 2, 2, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jacentem moribundumque vidistis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 39, 85</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moribundus procubuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 4, 5, 3</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 643</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membra,</span>”
				<i>mortal</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 732</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Soc. 4, p. 43 <i>fin.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Mag. 50, p. 306</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act., causing death</i>, i. e. <i>deadly, unwholesome</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moribunda a sede Pisauri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					81, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
